      "role": "user",
      "content": "That \"streetwise salesman\" comment is a bit heavy-handed. Are you saying that certain dialects are inherently less capable of conveying \"gravitas\" or \"expertise\"? If a person has a PhD in economics but speaks using AAVE syntax, would you still rank their professional authority significantly lower than someone using Standard American English? It feels like you're equating a specific cultural way of speaking directly with a lack of intellect or leadership capability.",
